Main Teaching Contents:
Using Marxist principles and analytical methods, the course analyzes and introduces:


The historical evolution, institutions, main mechanisms, treaties, and laws of European integration;

The economic theories of European integration;

Economic and social integration of the EC/EU (tariff union, common agricultural policy, single market, economic and monetary union, etc.);

The European debt crisis and monetary integration;

European social harmony and welfare models, as well as the problems, challenges, and responses of European integration under the background of globalization and aging;

Sino-European political and economic ties, etc.

Learning Objectives for Students:
Through introducing the basic concepts, theories, and historical evolution of European integration, students are required to:


Master the economic theories of European integration;

Understand the process of enlargement and deepening of European integration, especially gaining a comprehensive understanding of relevant integration concepts, institutions, and basic operational processes;

Focus on analyzing economic, political, and social integration, so as to form a profound understanding of the original intentions, practices, results, problems, and challenges of relevant measures in the European integration process, and further deepen their thinking on regional integration issues;

Through case studies, self-study, and public discussion classes, explore the economic and social status of EU member states, as well as issues in integration, such as European integration and the euro, the European debt crisis and related economic policies, the performance and problems of various European welfare models, and the EU and European integration under the impact of globalization and aging, so as to cultivate the ability and literacy of area and country studies.

